# Core Institutional Capabilities

## Governance

Purpose

Provide strategic direction, accountability, policy coherence, and institutional continuity.

Capabilities

- Executive Coordination
- Policy Design
- Regulatory Oversight
- Strategic Planning
- Public Accountability

---

## Procurement

Purpose

Allocate public resources efficiently while creating national capability.

Capabilities

- Strategic Procurement
- Supplier Governance
- Contract Management
- Value for Money
- Industrial Development

---

## Public Finance

Purpose

Convert national revenue into productive public investment.

Capabilities

- Budget Coordination
- Fiscal Governance
- Treasury Management
- Revenue Administration
- Investment Prioritization

---

## Digital Public Infrastructure

Purpose

Provide the digital operating layer for government.

Capabilities

- Digital Identity
- Authentication
- Digital Payments
- Data Exchange
- Government Interoperability

---

## Institutional Memory

Purpose

Ensure institutions continuously learn rather than repeatedly restart.

Capabilities

- Knowledge Preservation
- Policy Archives
- Evidence Management
- Organizational Learning
- Decision Traceability

---

## AI Governance

Purpose

Ensure artificial intelligence strengthens institutions without weakening accountability.

Capabilities

- Human Oversight
- Explainability
- Transparency
- Auditability
- Risk Monitoring

---

## Coordination

Purpose

Synchronize institutions across government.

Capabilities

- Cross-Ministry Coordination
- Multi-Level Government Coordination
- Public–Private Coordination
- Development Partner Coordination
- Crisis Coordination

